I'm a former "nethacker" on Nethack 3.0j.  I've been away from the game for a
while and recently picked up Nethack 3.1.3.  I've found a lot of similarity
between the new version and the previous one, as well as a *LOT* of really
interesting differences.  On the whole, I find the new version a pleasant
(though often brutal) change from the previous one.

Obviously, I've noticed several significant differences.  I'm not too concerned
about "operational" differences such as changes in behavior of some of the
objects.  I can discover most of these through the course of the game; some
were rather surprising and unpleasant, others were welcomed!

Right now, most of my questions concern the new multi-level feature.  Since
my questions are fairly specific and may constitute *SPOILERS* (To someone 
who has recently acquired the game and would prefer to discover these things
themselves), I'll protect my questions with the obligatory Ctrl-L...


Okay, here goes.

1.  I have encountered what appears to be a maze or mine level overflowing with
    dwarves, gnomes, etc.  Actually, it's an entire set of levels.  I've gone 
    down these levels until I hit "bottom", i.e., no more stairways down.  
    I've also encountered a town or village along the way.  When I get to the 
    "bottom", is there something specific I should do next or should I start 
    my way back up to rejoin the "regular" part of the dungeon?

2.  Inside one of the 2x2 gold vaults, I have encountered magic teleporter
    (I don't remember what it was actually called) that took me to some sort
    of castle or stronghold of Croesus.  Is there only one of these per game
    or do other 2x2 gold vaults have this teleporter as well?  If so, do you
    always go to the same stronghold or are there multiple strongholds?

3.  On another level, I encountered yet another magic transporter.  This one
    took me back to the "university" (I was playing a wizard at the time)
    where I conversed with my old teacher and was given a quest.  One of the
    things I noticed is that this level was labeled "Home 1".  Are there other
    "Home" levels as well?  If so, how do I get to them?  Is there anything
    of significant value here other than getting the "quest"?

4.  I cleaned out the castle, got my wand of wishing, and descended to the 
    level immediately below the castle, and entered what I think was called
    the "Valley of the Dead".  I couldn't magic map or teleport on this level
    and got hit by a zillion "undead"s and "&" type critters.  After wandering
    around for a while, I encountered the priest/priestess of Moloch, an
    unaligned deity.  This has the "feel" that I should do something special
    here, but I have no idea what that might be.  Chatting with the priestess/
    priest didn't tell me anything, nor do I have any indication that I am
    close to my quest item (I was told I would know when I got close to it.).
    In Nethack 3.0, what I would normally do is clear out the castle, descend
    one level and map it out, and then read a cursed scroll of teleportation
    (with teleport control) and descend to level 50 and work my way back up
    until I encountered the Wizard and the real amulet.  Have the "rules"
    changed significantly?  It looks to me like maybe they have.

I appreciate any info that anyone may have.  I really like the new version,
but I don't want to spend too much time floundering around wondering if I'm
missing something significant.

